&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text&quot; data-qa=&quot;message-text&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-block_kit_renderer&quot; data-qa=&quot;block-kit-renderer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;Reddit is a community of communities. It’s built on shared interests, passion, and trust, and is home to the most open and authentic conversations on the internet. Every day, Reddit users submit, vote, and comment on the topics they care most about. With 100,000+ active communities and approximately 130 million daily active unique visitors, Reddit is one of the internet’s largest sources of information. For more information, visit &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://www.redditinc.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://redditinc.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;www.redditinc.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is open to candidates based in the UK or the Netherlands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ads team is developing Dynamic Product Ads, enabling us to match users to specific advertiser products. Our vision is for Reddit’s product ads to be highly relevant and contextual. A user browsing r/golf sees ads for popular golf clubs. A user reading a thread on r/buyitforlife about sunglasses sees ads for the exact models being discussed, just a few clicks away from a purchase. To achieve this vision, we need a highly scalable catalog infrastructure and intuitive user experience to onboard thousands of advertisers and ingest millions of products into our systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Engineering Manager for the Product Catalogs team at Reddit, you will lead the full stack team responsible for our entire advertiser-facing experience. You will build UIs, APIs, and backend systems that manage advertiser’s products. The team also works closely with the knowledge graph teams to power organic shopping. This role combines technical expertise, leadership abilities, and drive to understand and deliver on customer needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a world class catalogs system that can scale to support billions of products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product managers and designers to craft compelling user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a wide range of teams from Ad Formats to Ad Delivery to ensure successful end-to-end delivery of product ads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and manage to SLAs within your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a strong mentor and cross-functional advocate for your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute meaningfully to team strategy. We give everyone a seat at the table and encourage active participation in planning for the future. Don’t just come along for the ride.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in backend or full stack product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience managing engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re highly technical, enough to solve almost any problem your team has yourself, but you prefer to guide your team into solving them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently. You’ll be working with stakeholders that are mostly based in North America. You need to be able to make decisions and solve problems autonomously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills. You must be able to collaborate effectively with teams in a fully-remote environment and discuss complex topics with technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Benefit programs that fit your lifestyle, from workspace to professional development to caregiving support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family Planning Support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gender-Affirming Care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Health &amp;amp; Coaching Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Group Personal Pension Scheme with Employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical and Dental Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Income Replacement Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bike to Work scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Vacation &amp;amp; Paid Volunteer Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;In select roles and locations, the interviews will be recorded, transcribed and summarized by artificial intelligence (AI). You will have the opportunity to opt out of recording, transcription and summarization prior to any scheduled interviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;During the interview, we will collect the following categories of personal information: Identifiers, Professional and Employment-Related Information, Sensory Information (audio/video recording), and any other categories of personal information you choose to share with us. We will use this information to evaluate your application for employment or an independent contractor role, as applicable.&amp;nbsp; We will not sell your personal information or disclose it to any third party for their marketing purposes.&amp;nbsp; We will delete any recording of your interview promptly after making a hiring decision.&amp;nbsp; For more information about how we will handle your personal information, including our retention of it, please refer to our &lt;a href=&quot;https://redditinc.com/policies/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy for Potential Employees and Contractors&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Reddit is proud to be an equal opportunity employer, and is committed to building a workforce representative of the diverse communities we serve.&amp;nbsp; Reddit is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If, due to a disability, you need an accommodation during the interview process, please let your recruiter know.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Data Center Operations Implementation Manager to own the end-to-end Day 0 to Day 2 transition of Nscale&#39;s data centres — spanning construction, fit-out, and live, steady-state local operations — across an assigned region and set of sites. Rather than owning construction execution itself, you&#39;ll be the connective tissue between Construction, Network Engineering, Compute/Infrastructure Deployment, and local Operations teams — driving a structured, well-documented transition so every site goes live on schedule and ready to support production workloads. This is an individual-contributor role built on strong stakeholder management, cross-functional influence, and travel to sites during critical transition windows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day 0 to Day 2 Transition Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end Day 0 to Day 2 transition process for each data centre site within your assigned region — spanning construction, fit-out, and steady-state operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain a standardized transition framework and readiness checklist applied consistently across your assigned sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and drive closure of cross-team action items, dependencies, and blockers standing between construction handover and operational go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate risks to go-live timelines, and drive resolution across the relevant stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track progress and status across Construction, Network Engineering, Compute/Infrastructure Deployment, Facility Engineering, SDM, and local site Operations teams throughout the transition window.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Construction teams to track handover status, outstanding items, and site readiness milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track Network Engineering&#39;s buildout, testing, and cutover activities required for a site to go live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track hardware intake, rack-and-stack, and deployment scheduling with Compute/Infrastructure Deployment teams to stay aligned with the transition timeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Facility Engineering on site systems and infrastructure readiness ahead of transition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with the Service Delivery Management (SDM) team to ensure alignment with customer needs, SLAs, security, and facility performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in regular cross-functional syncs and stakeholder reviews to stay current on transition status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a shared sense of ownership and accountability across stakeholder teams, even without formal authority over them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local Day Two Operations Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with local Operations leads to confirm staffing, training, tooling, and support processes are in place before a site transitions to Day 2 ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and validate standard operating procedures (SOPs) and operational processes required for local Operations teams to run the site post-handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create the operational site tool bill of materials (BOM) required for local Operations teams to maintain the site post-handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify the spare parts bill of materials (BOM) is complete and in place ahead of Day 2 handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate structured knowledge transfer and handover documentation from Construction, Network, and Compute teams to local Operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm monitoring, ticketing, and ITSM processes are validated and operating before a site is handed to local Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an escalation point for local Operations teams during the early post-handover period to smooth the transition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability, Safety &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce Day 2 readiness criteria that a site must meet before transitioning to local Operations ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate root-cause analysis for transition delays or gaps surfaced during handover, and drive remediation across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure health, safety, and environmental requirements are validated and documented as part of readiness sign-off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support certification and audit readiness (ISO 27001, ISO 22237, SOC 2, Cyber Essentials Plus, ISO 22301) ahead of go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor &amp;amp; Supplier Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with construction contractors and colocation providers as needed to close out remaining items affecting the transition timeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track vendor commitments and SLAs relevant to the transition window, and escalate delays that put go-live at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the Supply Chain team to align hardware intake and staging with the transition schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitoring, Reporting &amp;amp; Analytics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track KPIs and KRIs for the Day 0 to Day 2 transition process (time to transition, readiness checklist completion rate, post-handover incident rate, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dashboards that track transition status across your assigned site pipeline for all stakeholder teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce regular reports for senior leadership on transition status, risks, and blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data-driven insights to identify systemic bottlenecks in the Day 0 to Day 2 process and drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-8 years of experience in data centre operations, program/project management, or infrastructure deployment at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record coordinating the transition of new sites into live operations across construction, network, compute, and operations functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in a matrixed environment, influencing outcomes without direct authority over every stakeholder team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success managing multiple concurrent site transitions in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in hyperscale, cloud, or HPC data centre environments (preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Knowledge &amp;amp; Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of data centre power, cooling, networking, and compute infrastructure, sufficient to coordinate effectively across specialist teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with network deployment and cutover processes, and compute/hardware deployment lifecycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Layer 1 network infrastructure, including fiber, copper, optics, and transceivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ITSM tooling, ticketing systems, and monitoring platforms used by local Operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence and align Construction, Network, Compute, and Operations teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional communication skills, able to translate technical detail between teams with different priorities and vocabularies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program management discipline, with the ability to track and drive multiple concurrent workstreams to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in ambiguous, matrixed, fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bias toward ownership, pragmatism, and delivering results with urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous tracking of readiness checklists, risk logs, and action items across many concurrent site transitions within your assigned region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and refine standardized transition frameworks that scale with business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail in transition documentation and handover packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel to sites during critical transition windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
